var JOKES=["Why was the equal sign so humble? Because it knew it wasn't less than or greater than anyone.","Parallel lines have so much in common. It's a shame they'll never meet.","I'd tell you a joke about infinity, but it doesn't have an ending.","Why did the student wear glasses in maths class? To improve di-vision.","Six is afraid of seven, because seven eight nine. But nine was just following the order of operations."];
var FACTS=["A googol is 1 followed by 100 zeros — the company Google is named after it.","If you shuffle a deck of cards properly, that exact order has almost certainly never existed before: 52! ≈ 8 × 10⁶⁷.","The SAT never needs a calculator for more than about a third of the Math questions — spotting structure is usually faster.","Zero was invented as a number in India; the word “algebra” comes from the Arabic al-jabr, “putting back together”.","In a room of just 23 people there's a better-than-even chance two share a birthday."];
